  "query_preview": "..\nAn upper ridge will build into the area today with clouds and any\npatchy morning fog gradually dissipating from west to east. With \nthe light winds, things will happen slowly but the sun should warm\nthings to near normal levels with highs in the upper 40s to the\nmid 50s.\n\nClear skies and light winds are expected tonight. This may allow\npatchy fog to develop again, mainly in the river valleys. Low will\nbe 20s to low 30s.\n\nThe upper ridge will linger into Thursday before an upper trough\npushes in Friday. A weak cold front moves in Friday night with a \nbreezy day expected for Saturday. There may be isolated showers\naround but models are not in agreement with placement and/or\ntiming yet. This front should help to mix the atmosphere and warm\ntemps above normal starting Friday.\n\nAn upper ridge returns late in the weekend for dry and continued\nmild conditions. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was mainly used with this package but added the patchy fog for\ntonight in the Milk, Missouri and part of the Big Muddy valleys.\nTFJ",
